          "caption": "Distant view of Fes Jdid and the Royal Palace, seen from the south.\n(This is a crop and edit from a larger photo so unfortunately the resolution isn't high. On the right is a tall structure in the palace, probably the Dar al-Ayad al-Kebira, first built by Sultan Mohammed ben Abdallah. The huge structure with the pyramid roof on the left is probably recent, because it doesn't appear in early 20th century photos of the palace; there's also an unidentified minaret visible in front of it, presumably a palace mosque.)",
