          "caption": "Distant view of Fes Jdid and the Royal Palace, seen from the east.\nIdentifiable landmarks, from left to right: Borj Sidi Bou Nafa (large fortified bastion); Dar Ayad al-Kebira (palace structure with two tall parts visible with pyramidal green cupolas) and the minaret of Lalla Mina Mosque behind it (barely visible, obscured by the palace structure); a prominent and central palace structure (the largest green pyramid roof); the minaret of the Lalla ez-Zhar Mosque (just right of the large pyramidal roof, less prominent than the other minarets); the minaret of the Hama Mosque; the minaret of the Moulay Abdallah Mosque (very faint, seen in front of some large factory building in the distance); the minaret of the Lalla Ghriba Mosque and behind it the minaret of the Madrasa of Fes el-Jdid; and the minaet of the Grand Mosque of Fes Jdid.",
